MembraneForger Source Distribution License Notice

This repository is a combined source distribution. MembraneForger-authored
files remain MIT-licensed. The bundled runnable pipeline also includes and
directly uses GPL-covered scientific components:

- `resources/vendor/mstool/`: GPL-3.0-only
- `scripts/insane_M3_lipids_new.py`: GPL-2.0-or-later

Because MembraneForger imports the vendored GPL-3.0-only `mstool` package into
the Python process and distributes it with the runnable pipeline, the combined
bundled MembraneForger pipeline is distributed under GPL-3.0-only terms. The
GPL-2.0-or-later INSANE-derived component is distributed, for the combined
pipeline, under its GPL-3.0-compatible option.

This notice does not remove or narrow the MIT license grant for
MembraneForger-authored files when those files are used separately from the
combined bundled GPL-covered pipeline.

Full license texts are retained here:

- `LICENSES/MIT.txt`
- `LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt`
- `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt`
- `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`
- `resources/vendor/mstool/LICENSE`

Third-party provenance and modification notices are recorded in
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, `LICENSE_DEPENDENCIES.md`,
`resources/vendor/mstool/MODIFICATIONS.md`, `docs/insane_modifications.md`,
`docs/runtime_provenance.tsv`, and `docs/third_party_inventory.tsv`.

External CHARMM, CGenFF, Rosetta, PyRosetta, ligand, and local scientific
resource trees are not part of this source distribution.
